From 29d9007a445de1eddb703c01df1cb2af0b6f402d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kreijstal <elektrischrainbow@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:08:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sqlite3: also load libsqlite3-0.dll on Windows

sqlite3dyn (used by sqlite3conn/TSQLite3Connection) loads sqlite3.dll,
the name of the official SQLite Windows binaries.  MSYS2 and other
MinGW builds name it libsqlite3-0.dll, so on MSYS2 every
TSQLite3Connection fails with "Can not load SQLite client library
sqlite3.dll" unless the program sets SQLiteDefaultLibrary itself (seen
with Cheat Engine's symbol database).

When the default library name fails to load on Windows, try
libsqlite3-0.dll.  The requested name is still what SQLiteLoadedLibrary
records, so repeated InitializeSqlite(SQLiteDefaultLibrary) calls keep
matching, and the unit interface (and its CRC) is unchanged.
---
 packages/sqlite/src/sqlite3.inc | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/sqlite/src/sqlite3.inc b/packages/sqlite/src/sqlite3.inc
index b44b3e0..070ce73 100644
--- a/packages/sqlite/src/sqlite3.inc
+++ b/packages/sqlite/src/sqlite3.inc
@@ -1411,6 +1411,14 @@ begin
   if result  = 1 then
   begin
     SQLiteLibraryHandle := LoadLibrary(N);
+{$IFDEF WINDOWS}
+    { MinGW/MSYS2 builds of SQLite are called libsqlite3-0.dll, the official
+      Windows binaries sqlite3.dll.  Accept the former for the default name;
+      SQLiteLoadedLibrary keeps the requested name, so repeated
+      InitializeSqlite(SQLiteDefaultLibrary) calls still match. }
+    if (SQLiteLibraryHandle = NilHandle) and (N = Sqlite3Lib) then
+      SQLiteLibraryHandle := LoadLibrary(UnicodeString('libsqlite3-0.dll'));
+{$ENDIF WINDOWS}
     if (SQLiteLibraryHandle = NilHandle) then
     begin
       RefCount := 0;
-- 
